hey i'm lucy and i love mass effect now  recently i sat in on an hour-long  presentation with bioware  about the upcoming mass effect remaster  and afterwards talk to key members of  the dev team  you'll be pleased to hear i asked very  nitpicky questions and have compiled all  the big details i learned  into this exhaustive list if you like  mass effect as much as i do  please consider subscribing we have an  exclusive interview with mack walters  about the creation of mass effect 2's  iconic suicide mission  and he even talks about some cut  characters so if you're a big fan like i  am  you'll get a lot out of it i'm not gonna  have a lot of footage of the actual  legendary edition here  so i will mark when it is and isn't the  legendary edition  all right let's kick off with the big  stuff gameplay changes to modernize  mass effect 1. let's start with combat  there's improved aim assist where the  lock on is a little bit stickier and you  can now keep locked onto targets while  you're strafing  there's finally a dedicated melee button  and yes weapons have been balanced and  tuned  across the trilogy but definitely more  so in one a huge change in combat is  that they've removed class  based weapon restrictions and aim  penalties that means you can't  train in weapons your class isn't  specialized in but you can still use  them  without being penalized what about that  inventory system though  well it's still being worked on at the  moment but from the way they were  talking about it i wouldn't expect big  sweeping changes  there is gonna be a more unified control  scheme across all three games though you  can still issue commands to your squad  mates and bioware is improving those  controls in mass effect 1 to be more in  line with how they feel  in mass effect 2. squad ai is being  improved so if you send your squad mates  over to cover they will actually get in  cover  now they're also improving enemy ai so  hopefully that means that  now every time we come across guest  we're not going to get completely rushed  by them  the hud now looks more modern cleaner  and a bit smaller  it's not right on the edges of the  screen anymore it's a little bit further  in  i did see some test footage where they  were clearly toying with changing it to  be more in line with mass effect 2 and 3  but they've dropped that it's the same  mass effect 1 hud  just cleaner animations haven't been  outright changed but they have bug fixed  a lot of them so the example that  bioware gave was a lot of the times  characters weren't necessarily looking  exactly where they were supposed to so  they fixed that  input camera and cover systems have also  been smooth to try and eliminate some of  that wonkiness you can get in mass  effect 1  and speaking of wonkiness the mako has  had  a few touch-ups to make it easier to  control which  i'm a little bit sad about because i  love that awkward old thing but i can  see why a lot of people want it  there's a ton of other small changes  that i absolutely won't have footage for  so i'm just gonna rattle through them  quickfire style in scope aim smoothing  cover pass rebalanced xp for the level  60 cap which means that you don't have  to do it in new game plus  a more consistent auto save thank god uh  improvements to boss encounters  improved cooldown for first aid mini  games are also being unified across all  platforms  you might remember that console had a  weird simon says thing and  pc had a ring thing that's going to be  unified but i'm not sure which one  we're going to be getting just yet they  also said they're going to be decreasing  the difficulty  and frequency of those minigames so  fingers crossed they'll do the same for  mass effect 2 for the safe opening and  hacking stuff because  too much okay that was a lot of gameplay  changes for mass effect 1 so let's move  to the rest of the trilogy  in particular story is there gonna be  additional story content added  no the devs did look at what was on the  cutting room floor  but unfortunately the stuff that was cut  from the games couldn't easily be put  back in for the remaster they would need  to have been built from scratch  so nothing new in the game however if  you'd like a look at some of the stuff  that did get cut including never before  seen characters  subscribe for our interview with mack  walters i've got two words for you  techno hippie elephant in the room time  which ending will you get well upon  finishing mass effect 3 in the legendary  edition  you will be presented with the extended  cut max said the extended cut provides a  lot more context  and to him is part of the canon  there's now a universal character  creator across all three games  which means that customization options  that were added in mass effect 2  and 3 are now available to you in mass  effect 1.  they've also added some new makeup skin  tones and hair styles  including more black hairstyles there's  also finally a unified female commander  shepard across the trilogy  the fem shop design wasn't finalized  until mass effect 3  so retroactively adding her back into  mass effects 1 and 2  was one of the first things the team did  when they approached the remaster  they adjusted her slightly modifying  that very powerful jawline and adding  things like wrinkles and paws  [Music]  alright the big techie one how is this  baby gonna look  and run well it'll be playable in 4k hdr  at 60 frames per second if you're  playing on ps4 pro  xbox one x ps5 xbox series  on pc though those frame rates will be  unleashed there'll be faster load times  across all platforms  so what does that mean for our beloved  elevators which is a weird sentence to  say but elevators are so  big in mass effect uh it means that  they've actually added a button so once  the level has loaded in  you can press it and skip the elevator  rides if you want to  but that music's so good why would  in terms of visual improvements you name  it and there is a decent chance they've  probably done it  for textures they used an ai uprise  program to upscale texture resolution  four times that's across the board but  some textures  even got improved up to 16 times in mass  effects 1 and  2 pretty much every character armor  outfit and weapon  were hand touched and uprezzed we got to  see a bunch of them in the presentation  and a few that really stuck out to me  were  zaid's face like that man looked  weathered you could see every wrinkle  the eye bags was so defined  he looked like a different character it  was really cool  thane as well the scales on his uh head  just looked really really good  another thing that they fixed that  really stood out to me even though it's  so small  is they fixed eyelashes so in particular  ashley  girl that clumpy mascara has gone like  it looks so much better  so when it comes to the actual levels  themselves everything was uprised with  the ai  and then the human artists went in and  made subtle tweaks and changes  to give all the levels a little bit more  life the dig site at eden prime they  moved the sun  around so you get the light coming  through the trees it looked really  really cool  um ferrous for example had was so much  more rich  in detail in vermeyer all the water  around that looked  actually like water it looked way more  realistic so  i think they did a great job if you want  a full list of the tech stuff that they  have gone in  and tweaked and changed or maybe added  to then i've got you  they've made changes too tone mapping  anti-aliasing volumetrics and fog  depth of field and bloom bucket depth of  field which they said was to enhance the  mass effect art style  subsurface scattering on the skin  ambient occlusion  which was actually only on in very very  select scenes  in mass effect 3. it's now present  across the whole trilogy  and there's probably other stuff in that  list that i didn't note down i forgot to  mention  but they've made a lot of changes  there's a brand new launcher to start  all three games from one place  at this screen you can pick which game  to play watch the credits  switch your profile and if you're  playing on xbox even uninstall specific  games  i'm not sure why you'd want to but  that's up to you they do have the  genesis comics so  when you finish one game you get brought  back to this screen and then you select  the next one you don't just roll over  into the next game it's not one  unified experience the collection  contains over 40 pieces of downloadable  content so that's story packs  armors weapons and alternate outfits so  yes that does mean you've got the dragon  age armor in there as well as the  genesis comics  however there's one piece of dlc missing  and that is pinnacle station  from mass effect 1. now if you played  mass effect 1  on ps3 you might remember that pinnacle  station wasn't there  it was actually because the source data  was corrupted i asked mac about this  and it's the exact same reason here  unfortunately which might have  consequences for achievements and  trophies  um but they weren't talking about that  mass effect 3 multiplayer didn't make it  into the legendary edition we knew that  however  according to project director mack  walters it was apparently on the table  at the very beginning  but it would have been so difficult to  implement he actually likened the amount  of effort it would take to put  multiplayer in this collection  to be on par with what it took to uplift  the whole of mass effect 1.  so it got cut so how does galactic  readiness work now  well it got rebalanced and caveat it's  still being tweaked right now  but mack was saying that it's much  easier to get the best ending  if you play through mass effect 1 2 than  three however if you just play mass  effect 3  you can still get the best ending you  just have to really max out everything  still being tweaked pc players are gonna  get a couple of nice  little additions and you won't believe  it  controller support finally  no more mods there'll be directx 11  support  21.9 support and like i mentioned  earlier an unleashed frame rate  there's no ray tracing in the legendary  edition but there are real-time  reflections so the quick explainer on  this one is that mass effect trilogy was  made in unreal engine 3  and the effort that it would have taken  to bring it into unreal engine 4 would  have been way too much for this project  but what they can do now is they can  leverage the more powerful consoles and  pcs and then each scene basically set up  a second camera and render the sequence  twice  and that's what they can use for the  dynamic real-time reflections  very cool ps5 and xbox series stuff now  when we talked to bioware they didn't  believe that there was going to be  tempest 3d audio support for playstation  5 but they did say  improvements have been made at the asset  level on sound effects so  in particular they mentioned the weapons  and guns and all those sound effects  will have been improved  the asset level not necessarily at the  system support level  also kind of sad but there is no special  dual sense stuff  there isn't quick resume there's also no  photo mode  but they were saying what they were  doing instead was leveraging the power  of the new generation of consoles and  pcs  to make all those load times way way way  faster  i wasn't lying when i said that would be  an exhaustive list of everything  in the mass effect legendary edition if  you love mass effect as much as i do  i know i've said it like twice now but  seriously you do want to watch the  interview with mark walters  so subscribe and stick around for that  i'm on twitter at lucy james games if  you want to come talk about gareth  vacarian with me  and if you don't then i should go  [Music]  you
 

